WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.301 --> 00:00:02.635 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-Thank you, everybody.

00:00:02.635 --> 00:00:03.069 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I, um...

00:00:03.069 --> 00:00:04.437 size:88% position:44%
I've got to be honest --
I'm a little bit envious

00:00:04.437 --> 00:00:06.072 align:start size:94% position:6%
of the people
who are visiting New York,

00:00:06.072 --> 00:00:10.210 align:start size:94% position:6%
because I live here,
and it is very expensive, man.

00:00:10.210 --> 00:00:14.514
The rent goes up every single
year, for no real reason at all.

00:00:14.514 --> 00:00:16.783
Every year, a landlord
knocks on your door and is like,

00:00:16.783 --> 00:00:19.719 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Wow. You're still
living in there?

00:00:19.719 --> 00:00:20.253 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:20.253 --> 00:00:23.189
I guess we made last year
too easy for you, huh?"

00:00:23.189 --> 00:00:24.791
They should really change
the slogan of this city.

00:00:24.791 --> 00:00:27.394
Like, "If you can make it here,
you could have owned land

00:00:27.394 --> 00:00:28.561 line:92%
in a lot of other places."

00:00:28.561 --> 00:00:32.298 line:92%
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:00:32.298 --> 00:00:35.301
"You could have had a house,
and a boat, and a real family.

00:00:35.301 --> 00:00:37.103 align:start size:94% position:6%
Why are you doing this
to yourself?"

00:00:37.103 --> 00:00:41.474
And if you ask people, they're
like, "Well, the pizza's good."

00:00:41.474 --> 00:00:42.042 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:42.042 --> 00:00:43.977 align:start size:94% position:6%
I need to know
where the pizza's that bad

00:00:43.977 --> 00:00:46.546 align:start size:94% position:6%
that New York rent
is the option.

00:00:46.546 --> 00:00:47.180 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:49.582 align:start size:94% position:6%
Pizza is just
bread, sauce, and cheese.

00:00:49.582 --> 00:00:50.250 size:88% position:44% line:92%
It's hard to mess it up.

00:00:50.250 --> 00:00:52.552 align:start size:94% position:6%
There's only two levels
of pizza --

00:00:52.552 --> 00:00:54.788 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
great and fine.

00:00:54.788 --> 00:00:56.356 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:56.356 --> 00:00:56.890 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Completely okay.

00:00:56.890 --> 00:00:58.892
I've never had a slice of pizza
so bad I'm like,

00:00:58.892 --> 00:01:00.860 align:start size:94% position:6%
"You've got to be
kidding me!"

00:01:00.860 --> 00:01:02.862 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:02.862 --> 00:01:04.831 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Get this out
of my face!"

00:01:04.831 --> 00:01:07.467
Everybody in this room
has had microwaved pizza.

00:01:07.467 --> 00:01:11.871 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's absolutely disgusting,
but it's pretty good.

00:01:11.871 --> 00:01:13.807 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:13.807 --> 00:01:17.343 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:18.144 --> 00:01:18.578 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I...

00:01:18.578 --> 00:01:20.113 align:start size:94% position:6%
I've been trying to stay away
from pizza.

00:01:20.113 --> 00:01:21.781
I'm trying to be healthier.
I started going to a gym,

00:01:21.781 --> 00:01:23.216 align:start size:94% position:6%
mostly because
I just got broken down

00:01:23.216 --> 00:01:25.418 size:81% position:41%
by all the billboards
and slogans, you know?

00:01:25.418 --> 00:01:26.586 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're walking
down the street,

00:01:26.586 --> 00:01:27.887 align:start size:94% position:6%
and there's just
giant billbaords

00:01:27.887 --> 00:01:30.790 align:start size:94% position:6%
of hot, half-naked
sweaty people

00:01:30.790 --> 00:01:32.759
glaring at you
with a slogan underneath, like,

00:01:32.759 --> 00:01:36.229
"Hey, anybody think about
having sex with you today?

00:01:36.229 --> 00:01:37.163 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:37.163 --> 00:01:40.800 align:start size:94% position:6%
Didn't think so.
Hit hat treadmill right now."

00:01:41.568 --> 00:01:43.670
When you are healthy, though,
there are a lot of benefits.

00:01:43.670 --> 00:01:45.839
Like, even just going to places
that serve healthy food,

00:01:45.839 --> 00:01:48.408 align:start size:94% position:6%
because they care
about how it looks.

00:01:48.408 --> 00:01:50.743 align:start size:94% position:6%
They want it
to be presented nice.

00:01:50.743 --> 00:01:54.481 align:start size:94% position:6%
Fast food places
do not care at all.

00:01:54.481 --> 00:01:55.782 align:start size:94% position:6%
All food from
a fast-food place

00:01:55.782 --> 00:01:58.284 align:start size:94% position:6%
looks like it was made
during a riot.

00:01:58.284 --> 00:02:00.854 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:02.055 --> 00:02:02.655 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
The bag...

00:02:02.655 --> 00:02:05.625 align:start size:94% position:6%
The bag is crushed.
Things are squished.

00:02:05.625 --> 00:02:07.327 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, is the manager
in an arm bar?

00:02:07.327 --> 00:02:10.497 size:75% position:38%
How is there mustard
on top of the bun?

00:02:12.699 --> 00:02:14.334 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
There's...

00:02:14.334 --> 00:02:16.703 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:16.703 --> 00:02:19.205 align:start size:94% position:6%
There are also --
there are also no fights

00:02:19.205 --> 00:02:20.940 align:start size:94% position:6%
at health-food places --
ever. Never.

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:23.910
Because nobody gets drunk
and wants an arugula salad.

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:25.011 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It doesn't happen.

00:02:25.011 --> 00:02:26.179 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:26.179 --> 00:02:27.480 align:start size:94% position:6%
Nobody is drinking,
and is like,

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:29.749 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Anybody else
thinking quinoa?"

00:02:29.749 --> 00:02:30.717 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Never.

00:02:30.717 --> 00:02:31.618 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:31.618 --> 00:02:35.355 size:88% position:44%
But people do get drunk,
and they want nuggets.

00:02:35.355 --> 00:02:36.156 size:84% position:42% line:92%
And they want them now!

00:02:36.156 --> 00:02:39.592
"Give me those nuggets now,
or I will dragon-kick you

00:02:39.592 --> 00:02:41.594 align:start size:94% position:6%
through that
drive-thru window!"

00:02:41.594 --> 00:02:42.962 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:42.962 --> 00:02:44.097 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
When you...

00:02:44.097 --> 00:02:46.266 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:46.266 --> 00:02:51.471 align:start size:94% position:6%
When you get a chance, YouTube
"vegan restaurant fight."

00:02:51.471 --> 00:02:52.005 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:52.005 --> 00:02:54.274 align:start size:94% position:6%
You can get to the bottom
of all those videos,

00:02:54.274 --> 00:02:56.276 size:84% position:42% line:92%
because there are none.

00:02:56.276 --> 00:02:56.876 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:56.876 --> 00:02:58.778 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then, YouTube
"fast food fights."

00:02:58.778 --> 00:03:02.682 align:start size:94% position:6%
Whoa! It is nine days
of video.

00:03:02.682 --> 00:03:04.951 align:start size:94% position:6%
You can't even watch it all,
because as you try,

00:03:04.951 --> 00:03:07.187 align:start size:94% position:6%
people just keep
uploading more.

00:03:07.187 --> 00:03:08.688 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:08.688 --> 00:03:09.622 align:start size:94% position:6%
It is hard
to be healthy.

00:03:09.622 --> 00:03:11.624 size:78% position:39%
Like, even if you get
health drinks, right?

00:03:11.624 --> 00:03:13.860 align:start size:94% position:6%
On the side of healthy drinks,
they have warnings.

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:15.361 align:start size:94% position:6%
They have warnings
on health drinks that say,

00:03:15.361 --> 00:03:19.265 size:75% position:38%
"Warning! Only drink
one of these a day."

00:03:19.265 --> 00:03:19.632 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Why?

00:03:19.632 --> 00:03:22.202 align:start size:94% position:6%
Why can you only have
one can of vitamins a day?

00:03:22.202 --> 00:03:24.103 align:start size:94% position:6%
There is nothing on the side
of a bottle of rum

00:03:24.103 --> 00:03:26.539 align:start size:94% position:6%
that tells you to calm down
at all.

00:03:26.539 --> 00:03:27.974 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:27.974 --> 00:03:28.374 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Nothing.

00:03:28.374 --> 00:03:30.610 align:start size:94% position:6%
The only things is says is
"Drink responsibly."

00:03:30.610 --> 00:03:32.278 align:start size:94% position:6%
What does that
even mean?

00:03:32.278 --> 00:03:32.946 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Light laughter ]

00:03:32.946 --> 00:03:33.880 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Hey, if you're
gonna get drunk,

00:03:33.880 --> 00:03:36.416 align:start size:94% position:6%
make sure you're doing
your taxes at the same time."

00:03:36.416 --> 00:03:38.818 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:38.818 --> 00:03:41.120 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:42.755 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Have a few shots
and go vote.

00:03:42.755 --> 00:03:45.391 align:start size:94% position:6%
Make this a
responsible night."

00:03:45.391 --> 00:03:47.427 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is how hard
it is to be healthy --

00:03:47.427 --> 00:03:50.830 align:start size:94% position:6%
apples can kill you.
Apples!

00:03:50.830 --> 00:03:54.467
I read a thing that said that
apples soak up pesticides.

00:03:54.467 --> 00:03:58.104 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, if eat a lot of apples,
you can die.

00:03:58.104 --> 00:04:00.440 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, an apple a day
can literally bring a team

00:04:00.440 --> 00:04:02.942 align:start size:94% position:6%
of doctors
running your way...

00:04:02.942 --> 00:04:03.676 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:03.676 --> 00:04:06.579 align:start size:94% position:6%
...screaming
"Put the apple down!

00:04:06.579 --> 00:04:09.349 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're better off
snorting Doritos!"

00:04:09.349 --> 00:04:10.250 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:10.250 --> 00:04:12.852
If you are gonna be healthy, you
have to get organic food, right?

00:04:12.852 --> 00:04:15.555
Have to get organic food,
and that's so expensive.

00:04:15.555 --> 00:04:19.959
And organic food, at one point
in time, was just called "food."

00:04:19.959 --> 00:04:20.727 line:92%
It was just called "food."

00:04:20.727 --> 00:04:22.595 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then, they modified food,
and they were like,

00:04:22.595 --> 00:04:26.432 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Well, we can't call this
'modified food.'

00:04:26.432 --> 00:04:29.269 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, we'll call
modified food 'food'

00:04:29.269 --> 00:04:31.838 align:start size:94% position:6%
and food
'organic food.'"

00:04:31.838 --> 00:04:32.739 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:32.739 --> 00:04:34.707 align:start size:94% position:6%
Now, you've got to make
a real decision with yourself

00:04:34.707 --> 00:04:35.742 align:start size:94% position:6%
when you go in
the grocery store.

00:04:35.742 --> 00:04:38.011 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, "Do I want
the good strawberries?

00:04:38.011 --> 00:04:39.579 align:start size:94% position:6%
They're not gonna
hurt me.

00:04:39.579 --> 00:04:43.116 align:start size:94% position:6%
Nothing wrong with them,
but they're $5.

00:04:43.116 --> 00:04:46.352 align:start size:94% position:6%
Or do I want
the modified strawberries" --

00:04:46.352 --> 00:04:47.020 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
that are huge, too.

00:04:47.020 --> 00:04:48.921 align:start size:94% position:6%
They're pulsating
in the package.

00:04:48.921 --> 00:04:51.090 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:51.090 --> 00:04:53.793 align:start size:94% position:6%
You can't even
close the lid.

00:04:53.793 --> 00:04:58.298 align:start size:94% position:6%
They're picking fights
with blueberries beside them.

00:04:58.298 --> 00:05:01.567 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
But they're $1.75.

00:05:01.567 --> 00:05:02.302 line:92%
"It's been a rough month.

00:05:02.302 --> 00:05:05.405
I hope these strawberries
don't attack my kids."

00:05:05.405 --> 00:05:06.873 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thank you very much,
everybody.

00:05:06.873 --> 00:05:07.840 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Appreciate you.

00:05:07.840 --> 00:05:09.075 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Have a good night.

00:05:09.075 --> 00:05:13.012 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
♪♪♪♪

00:05:17.116 --> 00:05:18.551 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Oh, my gosh.

00:05:18.551 --> 00:05:20.186 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Nathan Macintosh.

00:05:20.186 --> 00:05:22.155 size:78% position:39% line:92%
You can see him at...

00:05:22.155 --> 00:05:26.993 size:81% position:41%
